<title>ISRAEL: Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</title>
<headline>Israel grain, meal, soy arrivals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following shipments of grain have arrived or are due to arrive in Israeli ports, according to the inspection agency Hevra Klalit Lehashgaha (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	     ETA	   Cargo	    Quantity   Origin</p>
<p>Gankis.K	   unloading   sorghum	  19,423     U.S.</p>
<p>				     wheat	    20,871</p>
<p>				     corn		8,501</p>
<p>Evandros.K	 unloading   tapioca	  18,000     Thailand</p>
<p>Liberty Sun	arrived     wheat	    42,141     U.S.</p>
<p>				     corn		8,691</p>
<p>				     corn screening  5,363</p>
<p>Bodaybo	    arrived     feed wheat	2,200     Europe</p>
<p>Klia		 arrived     corn	     33,872     U.S.</p>
<p>				     sorghum	   8,432</p>
<p>				     soya	     11,953</p>
<p>				     wheat	     8,827</p>
<p>Volgodon 5043    arrived     maize grits     3,540     Europe</p>
<p>DNPER 2	    arrived     sunflower meal  1,722     Europe</p>
<p>Jatay		arrived     bran		2,200     Europe</p>
<p>Volgobal 233	2/4	  feed wheat	2,500     Europe</p>
<p>Matushenko	  2/4	  maize grits     2,900     Europe</p>
<p>Omsky 139	   3/4	  feed wheat	2,750     Europe</p>
<p>Baltisky 69	 8/4	  feed wheat	2,500     Europe</p>
<p>Southern Venture  9/4	  corn	     22,357     U.S.</p>
<p>				     soya	     15,700</p>
<p>Ivan Kudria	10/4	  maize grits     3,000     Europe</p>
<p>Abusten	    11/4	  rapeseed meal   5,300     n/a</p>
<p>Liberty Sea	20/4	  n/a		60,000     U.S.</p>
<p>Liberty Spirit   28/4	  n/a		60,000     U.S.</p>
